{
  "_comment": [
    "The shared markdown corpus: one sample of each construct the Codex",
    "markdown dialect covers, with the document it must produce.",
    "",
    "Two converters read this file. internal/core/wiki/doc's",
    "markdown_corpus_test.go checks the SERVER's converter (goldmark with",
    "GFM, which turns a legacy markdown page into a document on first",
    "edit). web/src/lib/codex/markdownPaste.test.ts checks the EDITOR's",
    "paste converter. Neither is checked against the other's reputation;",
    "both are checked against these bytes.",
    "",
    "That is the whole reason the file exists. There were already two",
    "markdown dialects in this system — the server's converter and",
    "TipTap's type-time input rules — and a paste path is a third place",
    "the same text can enter a document. Three implementations that agree",
    "by inspection agree until somebody edits one of them.",
    "",
    "A construct absent from this corpus is a construct the paste",
    "converter does not claim. It stays plain text, which loses nothing:",
    "the source markdown is still there to be read and fixed by hand.",
    "",
    "The `doc` values were GENERATED from the server's converter rather",
    "than written by hand, so the corpus records what goldmark actually",
    "produces. Regenerate rather than hand-edit if the server's dialect",
    "ever legitimately changes."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "heading-1",
      "why": "the commonest construct in a pasted README",
      "markdown": "# Runbook",
      "doc": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "attrs": {
              "level": 1
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Runbook"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
